  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 accuracy. The image-only resnet50 baseline was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image branch contributes limited signal. The most logical single-variable extension is to test whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can improve the multimodal fusion. config_039 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) identical to the current best. This isolates the effect of image representation quality. Given that weighted fusion and transformer aggregation are already validated as optimal, and scvi_n200 is clearly the best RNA encoder, upgrading the image encoder is the highest-value remaining question. With only 1 experiment left after this, testing the most promising single improvement to the current best is the best use of the budget."
